      "description": "Playing Breeding Pool Turn 1 instead of Hushwood Verge limits Turn 2 options. If Breeding Pool enters tapped (correct since nothing to cast T1), then Turn 2 Hushwood Verge only provides G+G, meaning Doc Aurlock (GU) can't be cast Turn 2. Playing Hushwood Verge first, then Breeding Pool Turn 2 (paying 2 life) provides G+GU, enabling the powerful Doc Aurlock on curve.",
