      "description": "Feed the Cycle was used to destroy the opponent's earthbent Hallowed Fountain (a 1/1 land creature) instead of the Badgermole Cub (2/2). The Badgermole Cub is a much more significant threat — it provides mana acceleration (extra {G} when tapping creatures for mana) and is an actual creature that can attack. Destroying the Hallowed Fountain only removes a 1/1 body, and when an earthbent land dies, it returns to the battlefield tapped — so the opponent doesn't even permanently lose the land. The Badgermole Cub is permanently destroyed and represents far more board impact.",
